          <td>Inside the two-app box, 108 to 940 across and 288 to 1436 down</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">End card and call to action</th>
          <td>Out of the lowest 380 pixels and the top 288 pixels</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Right side of frame</th>
          <td>Keep faces and text left of 940 pixels, since no Douyin rail width is published</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Cover</th>
          <td>Export a separate 9:16 cover at 1080 by 1920</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">File</th>
          <td>MP4, sized well under 1GB, the smallest cap in circulation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Duration</th>
          <td>Confirm the ceiling in your own account before cutting a long edit</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Sound</th>
          <td>Burn in captions so the edit works either way</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>The <a href="/solutions/platforms/douyin">Douyin platform page</a> covers producing for Douyin specifically, the <a href="/services/design/short-video">short video design service page</a> covers the vertical edit itself, and the <a href="/resources/insights/rednote-note-cover-specs">article on RedNote note and cover specs</a> covers the same crop problem on RedNote.</p>

  <p>Reviewed 10 September 2026. Confirm every figure in your own creator account before building a batch to it.</p>

